<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Zero-shot Video Question Answering</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the advanced video language models on the open-ended video question-answering tasks under a zero-shot setting. The benchmark is composed of three datasets, involving ActivityNet-QA, MSRVTT-QA, and our newly proposed InternVid-QA. For a fair evaluation of the open-ended answers, we follow Video-ChatGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> to use GPT-3.5 to evaluate the accuracy (True/False) and quality score (from 0 to 5). We compare the performances of several advanced large video-language models, including Video-ChatGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, LLaMA-Adapter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>, Video-LLaVA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, LLaMA-VID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, MiniGPT-4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite>, MiniGPT4-Video <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> and VideoChat2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>. These competitors all conduct zero-shot video question answering conditioned on a single video. As mentioned above, our method’s answering is conditioned on the target video and several retrieved videos from the test set. According to the experimental results in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.1 Experiment Setup ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Enhancing Video Large Language Models with Structured Multi-Video Collaborative Reasoning (early version)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, our framework improves the baseline (Video-LLaVA) by 2.6% on MSRVTT-QA, 1.6% on ActivityNet-QA and 3.9% on InternVid-QA, which shows its capability to effectively integrate multi-video knowledge and provide more reliable answers.</p>
</div>
